  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **I Could Never Take The Place of Your Man** (1 review): The Prince cover runs just over seven minutes and is played very tightly [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **I Could Never Take The Place of Your Man**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **I Will Sing To You**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **It's About Twilight Now**: back after 21 archived shows (616 days) [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: What a Wonderful Man, Off the Record, Don Dante [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2005-06-04.ak40.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 15 songs; 94 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Recording has strong, full low end and the performance is well played [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer, who attended, ranks it among the best shows they have ever seen [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2005-06-04.ak40.flac16**: taped by Joe Waldron; transferred by Joe Waldron; source: Neumann ak40 > lc3 > km100 > m148 > 722 (24/96 kHz.) (~25', dfc, nos) [1]. Also: Fades were added at the start and end of the sets using WaveLab 5.0 [1]",
